      <title>GearVault - Walkthrough</title>
      <link>https://nvru.github.io/walkthrough/hsm/gearvault/</link>
      <pubDate>Sat, 21 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      
      <guid>https://nvru.github.io/walkthrough/hsm/gearvault/</guid>
      
      <description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;overview&#34;&gt;Overview&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Attacker IP:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;code&gt;192.168.211.2&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Domain Controller:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;code&gt;10.0.0.4&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Web Server:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;code&gt;10.0.0.5&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Difficulty:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;code&gt;Medium&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;OS:&lt;/strong&gt; Windows / Active Directory&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Creator:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.linkedin.com/in/marc-w-5346a3267/&#34;&gt;Marc W.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The objective was to enumerate the GearVault domain, gain initial access through a SQL injection in the shop web application, escalate to &lt;code&gt;NT AUTHORITY\SYSTEM&lt;/code&gt; on the web server using &lt;code&gt;SeImpersonatePrivilege&lt;/code&gt;, recover domain credentials, and pivot to the Domain Controller through Active Directory permission abuse and a backup operator account.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
